{
  "_comment": "The ShExMap extension's manifest vocabulary: what an examples manifest may write inside the mapping it binds to this file. A manifest binds it under a term of its own choosing and gives that term this file's URL as its property-scoped @context (JSON-LD 1.1): in the manifest's @context, `map: http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#` and, beside it, `map:parms: {@context: https://shexspec.github.io/extensions/Map/manifest-context.jsonld}`; an entry then writes `map:parms:` with these names bare inside it. The binding must name the term, not just the prefix: JSON-LD attaches a scoped context to the key as written, so a prefix alone would give map:parms its IRI but not its scope, and the mapping's contents would be dropped. Never import this file at the top level of a manifest: that would put these names in the outer scope, where they belong to nobody. Every name maps to an absolute IRI in the extension's namespace -- the one its schemas already use for %Map:{ ... %} semantic actions, `PREFIX Map: <http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#>`, so an implementation only needs one IRI to make sense of both -- and this file declares no prefix and nothing outside the scope, so it cannot collide with another vocabulary, whatever prefix the manifest chose for it. Outer names stay visible inside the scope, so the manifest core's pluginURL is written inside the mapping too, naming the plugin that implements this vocabulary. outputSchema(URL)/outputShapeMap(URL) name the materialization's target schema and root; staticVars are always-available globals handed to the materializer, written as a mapping from variable IRI to value, i.e. a node object whose keys are the variables themselves -- a nested blank node in RDF; expectedBindings(URL)/expectedOutputData(URL) are regression fixtures a test compares the run against; threadedOnly marks an entry that only ThreadedMaterializer-test exercises (its output has no legacy materializer to compare against). An X/XURL pair shares one IRI, the URL form typed @id, as the core's schema/schemaURL do. Stacked onto shex.js's doc/webapp-manifest-context.jsonld core. NOTE the namespace: http://shex.io/extensions/Map/# is the one extension IRI ending in #, so a term bound to it as map:parms is http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#parms.",

  "@context": {
    "outputSchema": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#outputSchema",
    "outputSchemaURL": {"@id": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#outputSchema", "@type": "@id"},
    "outputShapeMap": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#outputShapeMap",
    "outputShapeMapURL": {"@id": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#outputShapeMap", "@type": "@id"},
    "staticVars": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#staticVars",
    "staticVarsURL": {"@id": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#staticVars", "@type": "@id"},
    "expectedBindings": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#expectedBindings",
    "expectedBindingsURL": {"@id": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#expectedBindings", "@type": "@id"},
    "expectedOutputData": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#expectedOutputData",
    "expectedOutputDataURL": {"@id": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#expectedOutputData", "@type": "@id"},
    "threadedOnly": "http://shex.io/extensions/Map/#threadedOnly"
  }
}
